/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Functions: key, mbid, entry, draft, withAlbum, invalid, refused, load, loadV2
 *   Constants: actor, slotA, slotB, manifest, v1Fixtures, environment, previous
 * Tests
 *   - a valid Draft v2 parses to itself, and a draftless default is empty, unknown and public
 *   - Artist entries keep every primary before every featured entry and unique case-insensitive NFC names
 *   - Artist names reject controls, invisible formatting characters, lone surrogates and length or emptiness violations
 *   - Artist entry lists are bounded, need unique UUID keys and exact keys, and lowercase their keys
 *   - join phrases use the Credit phrase rules, and editing one never changes a role
 *   - Disc Numbers, Track Numbers and titles are bounded
 *   - Draft v2 keys are exact at every level, with one track per manifest slot
 *   - a client MusicBrainz ID is kept only when it equals the one stored for the same, unrenamed entry or label
 *   - the 48 KB cap refuses a growing draft but keeps a converted draft near the cap editable
 *   - value paths are only the Draft v2 paths of the manifest
 *   - a field save is 1 to 5 + 3 per file distinct changes, each exactly {path, base, value} with a valid value
 *   - an administrator save writes and marks only its changed paths, keeping other values and origins
 *   - a stale administrator-owned path refuses the whole save; an automatic one is overwritten; a matching value never conflicts
 *   - automation writes only empty or automatic values it still sees, never administrator values, and skips invalid ones
 *   - an Artist decision stays bound while its entry keeps its key and name; reordering, roles and phrases keep it
 *   - each Artist entry and the label keep their own decision: reordering, roles and phrases keep it; renaming or removing clears only it
 *   - a Luna Artist name becomes a one-entry primary Artist suggestion against the Draft v2 baseline
 *   - a legacy project converts to its Draft v2 view without touching its approval, histories, assets or analysis progress
 *   - the import detail shows Draft v2 values, entry- and label-bound decisions and every published identity, and offers work for format 1 and 2 projects only
 *   - an approval is format 2 only with one primary Artist entry, no label and a discNumber field (a Disc Number or null) on every track
 *   - every value path a draft has is addressable, so an absent origin always means the administrator
 *   - name and title bounds hold for the stored NFC form, so a saved value is never dropped from the editor view
 *   - a field save body is bounded before its fingerprint: item count, exact keys, path length, and each base and value as a draft value
 *   - value origins are stored under keys without dots, which every supported MongoDB release accepts
 *   - a stored value the editor view cannot show is replaced by a save from the shown value, while any other base stays stale
 *   - an approval is format 3 with entries of a key, name and primary or featured role, a named label or none, Disc Number fields, and 1 to 50 frozen Artists
 *   - a format-2 approval may leave every Disc Number unknown, as long as each track has the field
 *   - the approval digest binds the shown draft, decisions, cover and staged bytes in any key order, and nothing an approval does not show
 *   - converting a project saved before Draft v2 keeps its approval digest, so an approval built on its view stays current
 * @end-catalog */

/**
 * Draft v2 values, value origins and the legacy conversion. The parsers are the server contract for a field-patch save, the
 * value-state functions are the only two ways Draft v2 values change, and a v1 project converts deterministically without
 * touching its frozen approval. All names and identifiers are synthetic.
 */
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { after, before, test } from 'node:test';
// The database module loads first; importing adminImportService before it trips the index import cycle.
import '../../src/infrastructure/database';
